:Customer a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Customer" ;
    rdfs:comment "A person on Contoso's customer register: 104,990 of them, each with a name, a birth date and a place — continent, country, state, city. HALF HAVE NEVER ORDERED: 52,189 of the 104,990 appear on a sale, so the register is not the buyer list. The account is knowledge/customer.md." .

:Location a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Location" ;
    rdfs:comment "THE PLACE a store stands on — a country and a state, and nothing that belongs to the shop itself. Floor area, opening and closing dates are properties of PREMISES and live on Store; what a place owns is where it is. ONE PLACE MAY HOLD A SUCCESSION OF PREMISES over time, which is the fact this concept exists to keep separate from Store: `dim_store.store_key` declares `finer_than: location_code`, so premises roll UP into a place and a place never divides down into one. Summing a per-premises measure over a place that has been re-let counts it once per tenancy. A PLACE IS NOT A CITY IN THIS BUNDLE. Its finest geography is `state`, which in France means regions and overseas territories; `main.store` carries no city or town column. City exists only on the customer, as where a customer lives, and is declared personally identifying. No counts here, by the ruling of 2026-10-24 — they belong in data/profiles/dim_location.yaml where they can be re-measured. The account is knowledge/location.md." .

:Product a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Product" ;
    rdfs:comment "A thing Contoso sells, at the level the shelf knows it: a SKU. The account is knowledge/product.md." .

:Store a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Store" ;
    rdfs:comment "THE PREMISES Contoso sells from — a shop that stood on one place for one trading period, with its own name, floor area, opening date and closing date. It is what every sale is recorded against. A PLACE MAY HOLD A SUCCESSION OF PREMISES, so a store is NOT its place: see the Location concept for the place, and `dim_store.store_key#rulings.finer_than` for the declaration that one rolls up into the other. The account is knowledge/store.md. THIS DEFINITION CARRIES NO COUNTS, by the operator's ruling of 2026-10-24: \"you are disclosing values that variy through the time as constnts?!?!?! this is no go ... you can decribe things without constants too\". It used to say how many stores there were and how many were trading, which was a measurement of one day frozen into a sentence — and it disagreed with this concept's own `counts:` key, which is how one word came to name two grains. Counts belong where they can be re-measured: data/profiles/dim_store.yaml." .

:Order a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Order" ;
    rdfs:comment "One customer's purchase on one date, counted by distinct `order_key` over the line relation. It is also THE FACT NODE of the sales line, one row per order line - every money and quantity measure (net, gross, cost, discount, margin, units, and the per-unit prices) is a column it serves, and every edge from the sale to a dimension starts here. The account is knowledge/order.md." .

